ties by 12%. Most of it goes on substations and transformers (source: the `utility-capex-2027` document).\n- Pellham is the largest single buyer of grid equipment in Caldria.\n- Utilities make up 62% of VLTX holdings' orders. Pellham is 35% of those and Norvane 21%, so the two rising plans cover about 56% of VLTX's utility orders.\n- Financing is a risk. Utility bond spreads widened 30bp in Q3 2026 to 165bp, and equity markets have been less receptive. Norvane did price a C$1.1B bond comfortably. If financing tightens, capex could slip. Other nodes (n3, n5, n6) are assessing that.\n\n**Data centres: rising, but more slowly**\n- The data-centre outlook expects grid connection requests to grow 9% in 2027, slower than in 2026. It says power availability is limiting new sites.\n- Connection requests are only a proxy for equipment demand.\n\n**Limits**\n- The utility evidence covers only Pellham and Norvane. I found nothing on other utilities, order or backlog data, or the timing of the spending.\n- The data-centre view rests on a single source, with no equipment order figures and no 2026 baseline growth rate, so I'd put confidence at moderate.\n- The 2027 utility figures are plans, not orders placed.\n\nThe full answers are in n7.r1 (utilities) and n8.r1 (data centres).","ttft_ms":2702,"type":"result","duration_ms":31413,"uuid":"c389e55c-b9b3-437c-a343-29c9fe43f2a0","ttft_stream_ms":1303,"time_to_request_ms":466,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":47,"system_prompt":18,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":6,"input_attachments":63,"input_hooks":7,"conversation_append":18,"transcript_persist":34,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":60,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":20,"loop_entry":15,"message_prep":25,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":57,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":1,"tool_schema_build":18,"message_normalization":16,"client_creation":26,"request_build":30},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag